    "excerpt": "As previously stated, these systems depend upon each other for the running, maintenance and repair of the body as a whole entity.  The infrastructure of the human body is like a society: The glandular system is the government.  The nervous (electrical) system is the information highway, without which communication thro...",
    "fullText": "sneezing, coughing, sweating, aching, fevers, and diarrhea are experienced. — As previously stated, these systems depend upon each other for the running, maintenance and repair of the body as a whole entity.  The infrastructure of the human body is like a society: The glandular system is the government.  The nervous (electrical) system is the information highway, without which communication throughout the cities (cells, organs and glands) is crippled.  The police department consists of small immune cells called lymphocytes (white blood cells), neutrophils, basophils, and macrophages.  For added protection we have the military, which are the NK (natural killer) cells the large T and B cells.  Of course there are factories, like the liver, bone marrow, glands and some organs.  And trash pick-up and waste disposal are done by the lymphatic system, colon, kidneys, lungs and skin.  However, without general laborers a society would have all chiefs and nothing would get done.  The majority of the cells in the body act as laborers."
