    "excerpt": "The symptoms of hypothyroidism (low thyroid function) include: bone loss, improper bone growth, brittle and ridged fingernails, hair loss, cold hands and feet, a dislike of cold weather, heart arrhythmias, heart attacks, depression, connective tissue weaknesses, scoliosis of the spine, arthritis, fatigue, slow metaboli...",
    "fullText": "pigmentation. — The symptoms of hypothyroidism (low thyroid function) include: bone loss, improper bone growth, brittle and ridged fingernails, hair loss, cold hands and feet, a dislike of cold weather, heart arrhythmias, heart attacks, depression, connective tissue weaknesses, scoliosis of the spine, arthritis, fatigue, slow metabolism, obesity, hot flashes, cramping, spasms, myxedemas and growth issues.  The symptoms of hyperthyroidism (over-active thyroid) include goiter, protruding eyes, hyperactivity, thyrotoxicosis, and excessive-growth issues."
