    "fullText": "tissue. — Since most people choose to eat a predominantly acid-forming diet, over- acidic (acidosis) conditions of the body (both systemic and cellular) begin to take place.  Acidosis and inflammation are virtually the same thing.  Added to acidic diets are the acid-type hormones.  Females produce testosterone and a lot of estrogen, which are acid-type hormones.  Each month ovarian estrogen is produced in large amounts, which breaks down the inner lining of the uterine wall, causing the monthly menstruation cycle.  Men also produce the acidic hormones testosterone and androsterone.  These are aggressive-type hormones.  They effect many different cellular changes from the breakdown of tissue to the increased growth of tissue ...  all types of tissue, from hair (pubic, facial, etc. ) to muscle tissue.  These hormones affect sexual behavior, increase blood flow and cause erections."
