    "fullText": "Each divides into 2 to 11 alveolar ducts. — It connects with the epiglottis, hyoid bone, thyroid cartilage, vocal cords and cricoid cartilage at one end, and the trachea at the other.  TRACHEA (WINDPIPE) Your trachea is a 4. 5-inch-long cartilaginous tube.  The trachea bridges the larynx to the primary or main bronchi.  It extends from the sixth cervical to the fifth dorsal (thoracic) vertebra.  At this point it divides into two main bronchi, one leading to each lung.  The mucosa is made of ciliated epithelia that sweep mucus, trapped dust and pathogens upward."
