    "excerpt": "All foods and their constituents (like proteins, carbohydrates and fats) are mostly created from these basic elements, which are the building blocks that determine to what category molecules or compounds, etc. , belong.  These categories of molecular structures (such as sugars, starches, proteins, fats) make up the foo...",
    "fullText": "than that of raw foods. — All foods and their constituents (like proteins, carbohydrates and fats) are mostly created from these basic elements, which are the building blocks that determine to what category molecules or compounds, etc. , belong.  These categories of molecular structures (such as sugars, starches, proteins, fats) make up the foods that sustain life on this planet.  This chapter will view food and the process of eating from the perspective of chemistry and physics, and set it in the context of some overviews from God and nature.  Let’s first examine some of the most important constituents that your body requires to sustain, clean and repair itself.  There is among the Indians a heresy of those who philosophize among the Brahmins, who live a self-sufficient life, abstaining from eating living creatures and all cooked food.  — Hippolytus, Rome, 225 A. D."
