    "excerpt": "Free radicals are highly reactive and destructive compounds, which are by- products of metabolism, radiation therapy, tissue infractions, chemicals and foreign protein ingestion.  Oxidative free radicals can damage cell membrane walls, cellular mitochondria and cellular proteins.  This affects energy transport and the ...",
    "fullText": "New ones are being found every day, as humans will forever be discovering God. — Free radicals are highly reactive and destructive compounds, which are by- products of metabolism, radiation therapy, tissue infractions, chemicals and foreign protein ingestion.  Oxidative free radicals can damage cell membrane walls, cellular mitochondria and cellular proteins.  This affects energy transport and the DNA itself, leading to cellular mutations.  Free radicals also destroy enzymes, the key to all chemistry changes."
