    "excerpt": "Creation consists of opposites, and the movement of these opposites in relationship to each other creates electromagnetic energy.  Magnetism is where opposites attract and likes repel.  (If you have ever played with two or more magnets, you know what fun it can be to move magnets with magnets, and attract various mater...",
    "fullText": "Especially found in the leaves, bark, seeds and flowers. — Creation consists of opposites, and the movement of these opposites in relationship to each other creates electromagnetic energy.  Magnetism is where opposites attract and likes repel.  (If you have ever played with two or more magnets, you know what fun it can be to move magnets with magnets, and attract various materials to them. ) Whether you know it or not, you too are like a magnet, attracted to the opposite of yourself.  This “magnetism” helps you learn, and brings a balance to your experience in life."
