    "excerpt": "Water is one of the greatest catalysts for oxidation.  You see this in action when water combines with metals to create rust.  In our blood serum this oxidation creates electrolytes, which are conductors of energy.  Ionization creates both positive and negative ions.  Ions are your catalysts, like enzymes, which create...",
    "fullText": "the alkaline (cationic) and acid (anionic) processes in the body. — Water is one of the greatest catalysts for oxidation.  You see this in action when water combines with metals to create rust.  In our blood serum this oxidation creates electrolytes, which are conductors of energy.  Ionization creates both positive and negative ions.  Ions are your catalysts, like enzymes, which create action and reaction, or building and destroying.  Positive ions are sodium, potassium, magnesium and calcium, which are called cations.  Negative ions include chloride, sulfates, phosphates and carbonates, and are called anions."
