    "fullText": "FROM ALKALINE TO ACID Now, on top of all this, we cook (pasteurize) cow’s milk. — Or lymph node swelling, especially swelling of the tonsils?  The thyroid and parathyroid glands are located in the throat.  They also get congested with the mucus formed from dairy products, creating hyper- or especially hypo-conditions of these tissues.  The thyroid/parathyroid gland is responsible for calcium utilization by the body.  When these glands begin to fail from the mucus congestion, toxins and inflammation that dairy products create, your calcium utilization begins to fail—which is the opposite result for why you consume these products in the first place.  When a lack of calcium utilization at the cellular level begins, a host of conditions including depression, bone and tissue weaknesses, nerve and muscular weakness, and connective tissue weakness can also begin.  All are side effects from mucus congestion that has built up in our tissues from the use of dairy products.  Calcium is an abundant mineral."
