    "fullText": "parasites will naturally act upon this toxicity. — The acid or alkaline measurement in your body is classified in what is called pH factors.  The pH means “potential of hydrogen. ” The pH scale is 0 through 14—with 0 being the most acidic, 7 being neutral, and 14 the most alkaline.  Since each number on the scale represents a logarithm, there is a 10-fold difference between each number.  This can be very significant when you understand that the pH of the blood should be 7. 4, or slightly alkaline."
