    "excerpt": "There are many theories regarding what causes diabetes, from plaqued cholesterol around the beta cells, to autoimmune problems, to genetics.  Others say it’s from stress and obesity.  Every cell in your body is a genetic cell.  Some become weaker than others depending upon the above.  These weaknesses are magnified and...",
    "fullText": "Others say it’s from stress and obesity. — There are many theories regarding what causes diabetes, from plaqued cholesterol around the beta cells, to autoimmune problems, to genetics.  Others say it’s from stress and obesity.  Every cell in your body is a genetic cell.  Some become weaker than others depending upon the above.  These weaknesses are magnified and passed on through each new generation.  Because of our unawareness of this fact, the human species is currently facing serious tissue weaknesses, resulting mainly in chronic and degenerative diseases.  Remember there are only two causes of disease, any disease.  Number one is toxicity and number two is acidosis, in the form of inflammation.  These two causes are the effects of what you eat, drink, breathe, what you put on your skin, as well as what you think and feel.  These are the ways that you either strengthen your body or weaken it and the cells within it.  TREATING DIABETES I have always put diabetics on a raw fruit and vegetable diet."
