    "excerpt": "As you grew up, these timeless moments were lost at the hands of thought and desire.  The way teaching is done in most of our school systems promotes competition and limits free thinking, just as the materialistic world of possessions limits freedom and happiness.  These circumstances have greatly reduced our overall a...",
    "fullText": "One should start enjoying life for what it is. — As you grew up, these timeless moments were lost at the hands of thought and desire.  The way teaching is done in most of our school systems promotes competition and limits free thinking, just as the materialistic world of possessions limits freedom and happiness.  These circumstances have greatly reduced our overall awareness and our ability to experience God, the source of true vitality, happiness and bliss.  By detoxifying your physical body you can start a chain of events that will allow you to clean and bring under control your emotional and mental processes.  You can help this process by allowing old thought patterns and the emotions that can surface during detoxification to finally be released and forgotten.  There are several ways to do this.  Begin by watching your thoughts.  Step away from them and become the observer.  Become detached about the outcome of things and from other people’s opinions and emotions.  Let go.  Give it all over to spirit, God, the wind ..."
