    "fullText": "Fresh, uncooked foods, especially fruits, are self-cleansing. — their bodies with bad fuels—foods that leave a lot of residues in their tissues —they must clean the body out, or suffer the consequences.  Diseases are nothing more than signs and symptoms that reflect the body’s need to clean and rebuild itself.  Fresh, uncooked foods, especially fruits, are self-cleansing.  They not only feed the body, they keep it clean internally as well.  Detoxification is truly a science and an art unto itself; a necessary response to the consumption of toxic and congestive foods that have clogged and obstructed the human body.  In nature, detoxification is a continual process that all of life goes through, at one level or another.  The process of cleaning your body of toxins, mucus and acidosis can create symptoms that are seen as diseases by some doctors, and so we have been taught to fear this natural process.  All life in the physical world takes in energy, metabolizes it, and then excretes the remains and by-products."
