    "fullText": "It depends upon the individual and how toxic he or she is. — Paralysis of any part of the body Black mucus discharges from the lungs Heavy brown discharge or blood in the urine with associated kidney pain Heavy black discharge from the bowels with diarrhea Tumors popping out all over the body Loss of sight Loss of hearing Severe dizziness (or vertigo) Severe fatigue Abscesses developing all through the mouth Loss of fingernails or toenails Excessive weight loss (this can result when a pancreatic weakness exists) Severe shortness of breath (use an antispasmodic or inhaler) Temporary deep depression, released through crying, anger, laughter, etc.  Mental confusion Skin cracking open Teeth becoming loose (major) Old suppressed symptoms (like the case of “poison ivy”) reappear Most people do not experience this severe level of detoxification.  It depends upon the individual and how toxic he or she is.  How many medications a person is taking is also a factor."
