    "excerpt": "OTHER RAW FOODS Pecans Almonds Sunflower Seeds Sesame Seeds Pumpkin Seeds Coconuts Pine Nuts Note –Eat moderately of this category. Too many of these foods can be acid- forming, energy robbing, and will slow or stop the cleansing process. MODULE 7.2 Acid/Alkaline Food Chart All foods contain both acid-forming and alkal...",
    "fullText": "We have examined our species and the types of foods that best suit us. — OTHER RAW FOODS Pecans Almonds Sunflower Seeds Sesame Seeds Pumpkin Seeds Coconuts Pine Nuts Note –Eat moderately of this category. Too many of these foods can be acid- forming, energy robbing, and will slow or stop the cleansing process. MODULE 7.2 Acid/Alkaline Food Chart All foods contain both acid-forming and alkaline-forming elements. It is not the organic matter of foods that leave these acid or alkaline residues in your body. It is the inorganic matter or minerals that determine the acidity or alkalinity of the body fluids and tissues. Potassium, sodium, magnesium and calcium are considered the alkaline-forming electrolytes. Phosphorus, sulfur and manganese are the acid-forming elements. Several processes can be used to determine whether a food is more acid- forming or alkaline-forming. Generally, if a food has dominant acid-forming elements over alkaline-forming elements it’s considered acid-forming. The"
