    "excerpt": "There are only a few herbs to approach with caution, such as Peruvian Bark (Cinchona calisaya).  This herb is beneficial at low dosages, but toxic at high dosages.  I would leave herbs like this alone.  This chapter begins with a short essay ( Module 8. 1 ) on the common and traditional uses of botanicals, and then in ...",
    "fullText": "This book is aimed at changing your viewpoint about treatment. — There are only a few herbs to approach with caution, such as Peruvian Bark (Cinchona calisaya).  This herb is beneficial at low dosages, but toxic at high dosages.  I would leave herbs like this alone.  This chapter begins with a short essay ( Module 8. 1 ) on the common and traditional uses of botanicals, and then in Module 8. 2 provides a detailed list of some of the strongest and most effective herbs that nature has to offer.  These herbs have been clinically tested for many years.  The results of these herbs in supporting tissue regeneration have been miraculous.  We humans have a lot to learn when it comes to the power of botanicals to rebuild the body."
