    "fullText": "Has strong antioxidant power to help remove acids from the body. — A strong astringent, similar to witch hazel and white oak bark.  Useful for ulcerated conditions.  Helps remove toxins from the body.  Useful for prostatitis.  Use in cases of rheumatism.  Scientific name : Aesculus hippocastanum Parts used : Bark, dried horse chestnut seeds, dried horse chestnut leaves.  Actions : Anti-inflammatory, anti-rheumatic, astringent, bitter, cellular proliferator (especially to the vascular walls), expector ant, febrifuge, mild narcotic, nutritive.  Horsetail or Shavegrass Horsetail is one of the greatest herbs for bone and connective tissue weaknesses.  It is very high in silica, which is converted into calcium by the liver.  This herb has great healing powers to all tissues of the body."
