    "fullText": "It is an extremely good herb for the urinary tract (kidneys and bladder). — Use caution in cases of extreme kidney damage.  It is anti-inflammatory and has some anti-spasmodic properties.  It has antiseptic properties, which are useful in killing fungi, bacteria and yeasts.  Great for UTIs (urinary tract infections) and parasitic overgrowths in the GI tract.  It is also a natural diuretic, and relieves excess water.  Said to aid in restoring the pancreas, and beneficial in cases of diabetes, as it has natural insulin properties.  Scientific name : Juniperus communis or species Parts used : Usually the berries, also the oil (from the berries and wood), leaves, bark.  Actions : Anodyne, antiseptic, aromatic, carminative, diaphoretic, diuretic, emmenagogue, stimulant, stomachic."
