    "fullText": "contain type A or B antigens. — Decreased levels may indicate hypoglycemia, hypothyroidism, liver disease and Addison’s disease.  MINERALS — The minerals sodium, potassium, chloride and calcium are the main electrically-charged cations and anions, which constitute the body’s electrolytes.  SODIUM — Sodium is the most abundant cation (positively charged) mineral in extracellular fluids.  Therefore, it is the major salt in determining extracellular osmolality (transportation) of nutrients and constituents."
