    "fullText": "pineal gland synthesizes melatonin. — pineal gland synthesizes melatonin.  Melatonin is inhibited when light strikes the retina.  This small gland is considered by many to be the spiritual gland.  One of the seats or doorways for Spirit in the physical world.  Pituitary Gland a small, gray, rounded body attached to the base of the brain secreting hormones that regulate the thyroid, adrenals, and other endocrine organs.  It is often referred to as the “Master Gland” of the body and secretes a number of hormones that regulate many bodily processes including growth, reproduction and various metabolic activities.  Plaque a fatty, fibrous, cholesterol-containing mass in the lining of the arteries and other tissues.  The buildup of plaque in the arteries is a leading cause of cardiovascular occlusions, causing strokes and heart attacks.  Plaque deposits on the teeth can lead to gum disease.  Alzheimer’s disease is associated with the accumulation of plaque in the brain tissue causing a lack of nutrition to cells."
