    "fullText": "Freezing and refrigeration hinders enzymatic activity. — After presenting a host of evidence demonstrating that all living creatures have a fixed enzyme potential which can be (and usually is) prematurely exhausted, Dr.  Howell in Enzyme Nutrition writes: \"Humans eating an enzyme- less diet use up a tremendous amount of their enzyme potential in lavish secretions of the pancreas and other digestive organs.  The result is a shortened lifespan (65 years or less as compared with 100 or more), illness and lowered resistance to stresses of all types, psychological and environmental. \" The generational introduction of substances foreign to the organism causes eliminative organs (the bowels, kidneys, liver, skin, sinuses and lungs).  A purifi- cation of the diet enforces a self-healing and a radical, whole-body rejuvenation.  As you apply the health and diet system in this book, you may find that the common cold, flus, fever, grogginess, etc."
