    "excerpt": "There are three classes of enzymes: • metabolic • digestive • food Metabolic enzymes operate in all the cells, tissues, and organs and are an essential part of every biological activity.  Digestive enzymes are produced by, and appear in, the alimentary organs.  They help digest carbohydrates, fats and proteins.  Amylas...",
    "fullText": "Freezing and refrigeration hinders enzymatic activity. — There are three classes of enzymes: • metabolic • digestive • food Metabolic enzymes operate in all the cells, tissues, and organs and are an essential part of every biological activity.  Digestive enzymes are produced by, and appear in, the alimentary organs.  They help digest carbohydrates, fats and proteins.  Amylases are enzymes that digest carbohydrates.  Lipases are enzymes that digest fats.  Proteases are enzymes that digest proteins.  Food enzymes come enclosed with all whole raw foods in their proper propor- tions."
