    "excerpt": "Salad: 1 head of lettuce 1 large collard leaf 1/4 head of green cabbage 1 ounce (30 ml) of organic stone-crushed, cold-pressed extra virgin olive oil 1-2 avocados 10 strawberries Mix together and toss into a salad.  Eat this salad twice each day: once for lunch, once for dinner.  The high-calcium content of green-leafe...",
    "fullText": "100 j THE SUNFOOD DIET Or, if you are more active, try... — Salad: 1 head of lettuce 1 large collard leaf 1/4 head of green cabbage 1 ounce (30 ml) of organic stone-crushed, cold-pressed extra virgin olive oil 1-2 avocados 10 strawberries Mix together and toss into a salad.  Eat this salad twice each day: once for lunch, once for dinner.  The high-calcium content of green-leafed vegetables loosens constricted tissues.  Most back pain is associated with an acid condi- tion of the body - calcium counteracts and neutralizes acidity.  The strawberries are included because they contain organic salycilates, which are the basic ingredient of painkillers, such as aspirin.  For An Upset Stomach Or Ulcer Juice: 1/2 head of green cabbage 2 ribs of celery 2 apples Cabbage is rich in beta-carotene, vitamin C, sulfur, selenium and especially the amino acid glutamine.  Studies done by Dr.  Garnet Cheney, who at one time headed the Cancer Division of Stanford Medical School, revealed the value of glutamine in healing ulcers.  Dr."
