    "excerpt": "For example, the herbivorous cow has been fed the flesh of other dead cows, mixed in with its feed, for at least a century by the cattle industry.  Cows still continue to survive on such food.  Yet, an omnivorist would argue that the cow is no longer an herbivore, but is now an omnivore, because it can eat something as...",
    "fullText": "To a degree humans have adapted. — For example, the herbivorous cow has been fed the flesh of other dead cows, mixed in with its feed, for at least a century by the cattle industry.  Cows still continue to survive on such food.  Yet, an omnivorist would argue that the cow is no longer an herbivore, but is now an omnivore, because it can eat something aside from common grass."
