    "excerpt": "It is interesting to note that wild chimpanzees, who include animal food in their diet (mostly insects), do not exceed 10% animal food in their nutrition.  Unchecked levels of raw animal-food consumption seems to be associated with a poverty consciousness - a subconscious belief that killing, lack and hard- ship are la...",
    "fullText": "The dates for rock samples taken from the KBS Tuff were all over the place. — It is interesting to note that wild chimpanzees, who include animal food in their diet (mostly insects), do not exceed 10% animal food in their nutrition.  Unchecked levels of raw animal-food consumption seems to be associated with a poverty consciousness - a subconscious belief that killing, lack and hard- ship are laws of life.  Repeatedly thinking about demineralized food and deficiency is another facet of a poverty mentality.  Thoughts of lack create lack.  Thoughts of abundance create abundance.  Feelings of fear along with thoughts of lack, deficiency, and doubt lead one to create a reality and diet where those thoughts thrive.  A few people opt for raw-animal food because they sincerely need nutrients, others opt for this approach due to food addictions and an unwillingness to detoxify.  They want benefits without detoxification, but do not understand that something for nothing disobeys the karmic law.  They replace cooked-food stim- ulation with another kind - raw-animal food."
