    "excerpt": "152 | ORIGINS \"Trust in faith and Common sense Have no place In their science. They don't understand The reality they picture Is but a reflection — Of the thinker. Divine and regal, Is the grand-ancient world The creation riddle Cannot be unfurled. Out there is a different place, Older, greater, deeper by far Than the ...",
    "fullText": "152 | ORIGINS \"Trust in faith and Common sense Have no place In their science. — 152 | ORIGINS \"Trust in faith and Common sense Have no place In their science. They don't understand The reality they picture Is but a reflection — Of the thinker. Divine and regal, Is the grand-ancient world The creation riddle Cannot be unfurled. Out there is a different place, Older, greater, deeper by far Than the twinkling of The farthest star. The harm to the Earth Might be absolved, But her mysteries Will never be solved.\" ORIGINS | 153 They chewed on fruits In the soft, warm breeze. As a waft of smoke Caused a monkey to sneeze. \"Here they encroach On our Paradise Found They'll slash and burn this Place — to the ground. They don't think Beyond the fringe Of the tiny world They're living in. They cut then build Another sharp fence, When all they need is Water, leaves... silence. Materialist obsessions, The Survival of the fit Has turned the Earth Into a fire pit."
