    "excerpt": "The gorilla possesses a fantastic musculature and is capable of bench pressing 4,000 pounds (more than 1800 kg).  In his wonderful book, L'Homme, Le Singe, Et Le Paradis (Humans, Primates, and Paradise), Albert Mosseri describes: (Translation) \"The gorilla is not interested in eating so-called protein foods.  How can t...",
    "fullText": "Any cooked foods eaten should be properly combined. — The gorilla possesses a fantastic musculature and is capable of bench pressing 4,000 pounds (more than 1800 kg).  In his wonderful book, L'Homme, Le Singe, Et Le Paradis (Humans, Primates, and Paradise), Albert Mosseri describes: (Translation) \"The gorilla is not interested in eating so-called protein foods.  How can they develop all that muscle mass, weighing many hundreds of pounds, eating only green vegetables and fruits?  This fact is of great impor- tance."
