    "fullText": "They are alert, content, happy and eager to explore life. — Simple reasoning would suggest that eating less exposes the organism to less foreign materials, less toxins and less energy-draining foods.  It seems that as soon as one stops eating, all the toxins forced in through mucus pressure due to eating, especially toxic food, begin to flow out.  A coating on the tongue will form, one may feel unwell, weakness can set in, hypoglycemia (low blood sugar) will make its appearance and other symptoms will arise."
