    "fullText": "The more modern the fossil, the more tooth decay. — These struc- tural dental challenges begin essentially as birth defects and are exacerbated by continuous improper nutrition.  T. C.  Fry reported in an article entitled, \"The Myth Of Health In America\" which appeared in Dr.  Shelton's Hygienic Review (37:7, p.  150-152) that 98. 5% of the US population suffers from dental prob- lems of one type or another.  These may often be reversed and corrected in one or more generations of eating significantly more mineral-rich organic green- leafed vegetables, grass (wheatgrass), certain herbs (horsetail tea or bamboo sap) and other raw foods in general."
