    "fullText": "\"It is today easier to write books, preach and pray, saying I am an exception. — A large proportion of ordinary fasting attempts fail because of the ignorance of the fact that with the beginning of the mucusless diet the old mucus is being excreted so much more forcibly until that person is absolutely clean and healthy.  Thus the seemingly most healthy person has first to pass through a condition of sickness (cleansing), or go through an intermediate stage of illness to a higher level of health.  Growing old is found to be latent disease, a slow but constantly increasing disturbance in the opera- tion of the motor of life."
