    "excerpt": "Every time he exposes himself to the sun or eats the living cells of fruit, or engages in a fast all this dead matter is eliminated from his body.  However, the cure of fasting must be carried out with the greatest care.  Today's medications are designed to protect man from a breakdown of his cells but in most cases a ...",
    "fullText": "This is true but only so far as courage and knowledge are concerned. — Every time he exposes himself to the sun or eats the living cells of fruit, or engages in a fast all this dead matter is eliminated from his body.  However, the cure of fasting must be carried out with the greatest care.  Today's medications are designed to protect man from a breakdown of his cells but in most cases a doctor will only be consulted when the disease is imminent whereas very little if anything is done for prevention.  The vegetarians cannot deny that the meat and alcohol consuming portion of the population has produced a good number of healthy people, ca- pable of great achievements and longevity."
