    "excerpt": "CHAPTER 7 Building a perfect body thru fasting As long as the waste is in the circulation you feel miserable during a fast; as soon as it is thru the kidneys you feel fine. Two or three days later and the same process repeats itself. This will explain why conditions change so often during a fast, why it is possible for...",
    "fullText": "Two or three days later and the same process repeats itself. — CHAPTER 7 Building a perfect body thru fasting As long as the waste is in the circulation you feel miserable during a fast; as soon as it is thru the kidneys you feel fine. Two or three days later and the same process repeats itself. This will explain why conditions change so often during a fast, why it is possible for you to feel unusually better and stronger on the twentieth than on the fifth day, for instance. As this entire cleansing process (thru continued contracting of the tissuesbecoming lean) has to be done by and with the original old blood compo- sition of the patient, a long fast, especially a too long a fast, would be criminal if the sick organism is too greatly clogged up by waste. Fasters who died from too long a fast did not die from lack of food but died from their own waste, i.e. they actually suffocated. More clearly expressed: The immediate cause of death is not a lack of vital substances in the blood but too much obstruction. Obstruction becomes as great as or even greater than air pressure and, therefore, the body mecha- nism is \"deadlocked.\" FASTERS SHOULD DRINK LEMON JUICE EITHER UNSUGARED OR WITH A TRACE OF 75 PDF compression, OCR, web optimization using a watermarked evaluation copy of CVISION PDFCompressor"
