    "fullText": "Non-mucus forming food, i.e. — In fact, the waste products of meat, fatty plaque-shaped particles, are deposited on the walls of the blood vessels where in time they form a thick lining, calcify and thus contribute to the hardening of the arteries.  This hardening of the arteries, in many cases resulting in high blood pressure, is the chief cause of heart attacks and diseases of senility.  Tests on animals have already shown that meat-eating animals will die if fed on cooked meat alone.  And rats soon die if kept on a diet of white flour."
