    "fullText": "100 RATIONAL FASTING inside. — APPENDIX 101 instead of the thin persons, whose poisonous en- cumbrance is much less.  The fleshy ones are like pneumonia patients, suffocated (choked) by their own poisonous mucus or auto-intoxication.  Not a single faster dies or has died from starvation, but from his own self-poisoning, often enhanced by wrong diet as the fast ends.  Orange juice is often advised in this country, which is right in some cases, but for a heavily encumbered or fleshy patient it is quite dangerous.  Orange juice is an ideal food, but when mixed with the awful poison- ous mixture in the stomach of the faster, it adds to the quickness with which it is taken up by the blood, and is likely to harm the patient.  There is much to be learned about fasting and a mucusless diet, simple as it looks to a layman, for no two cases need just the same preparatory diet or length of fast, should be supervised by one of experience."
