    "fullText": "APPENDIX 107 clogged up system with mucus, whether sick or not. — 108 RATIONAL FASTING strict accordance with the condition of the patient, but to combine them as a \"Systematic Cleansing\" the success is remarkable and satisfactory.  The great difference between a diet of healing and a diet of nourishment seems to be almost unknown to both practitioners and laymen.  Fruit is the ideal, practical and natural diet of mankind, for nourish- ment, but the Mucusless Diet is a diet of healing and consists of raw and cooked fruits, starchless and leafy vegetables and mucus poor cereals spe- cially prepared.  A special or medical diagnosis is not necessary, nor the local name of the disease, but the amount of encumbrance of mucus and the activity of its toxins is of the first importance, and then, the degree to which the individual's encum- brance has affected his vital energy."
