    "excerpt": "128 RATIONAL FASTING Seen thru' the glasses of dietetics and fastinghygi- enic and dietetic rules, you will find that these ideas go, like a red string, thru' the Mosaic legisla- tionand thru' the stories of physical and spiritual heroes and prophets of the Old and New Testa- ments.  That physical culture in the classi...",
    "fullText": "You will, moreover, serve your country better in this way than in any other. — 128 RATIONAL FASTING Seen thru' the glasses of dietetics and fastinghygi- enic and dietetic rules, you will find that these ideas go, like a red string, thru' the Mosaic legisla- tionand thru' the stories of physical and spiritual heroes and prophets of the Old and New Testa- ments.  That physical culture in the classic age of old Greece was combined with fasting and a high standard of dietetics can be proved by the stories of two of the greatest geniuses of history: Pythag- oras and Hippocrates.  Pythagoras, an immortal mathematical genius; vegetarian and founder of a high-standing school of philosophy, went to Egypt to learn more about the \"secret sciences\" of that country.  Before he was allowed to enter into the school of the learned, called High Priests at this time, he had to undergo a fast of forty days, under supervision, outside of the city."
