    "fullText": "170 RATIONAL FASTING 3. — 170 RATIONAL FASTING 3.  The presence of unevacuated feces, retained through sticky mucus in the pockets of the intes- tines, constantly poisoning, and thereby interfer- ing with proper digestion and blood-building.  You will become convinced of this fact - of this diagnosis of your disease - by another surprise in store for you; if you will clean your intestines both before and after the test, with a harmless herb- vegetable compound.  To look inside your body - clearer and far bet- ter than can be done by doctors with their expen- sive X-ray apparatus - and learn the cause of your disease, or even discover some hitherto unknown physical imperfection or mental condition, try this: Fast one or two days, or eat only fruits for two or three days, and you will notice that your tongue will become heavily coated.  When this happens to the acutely sick, the doctor's conclusion is - \"indi- gestion. \" The tongue is the mirror not only of the stomach, but of the entire membrane system, as well."
