    "fullText": "General Introductory Principles L ESSON I. — Disease is an effort of the body to eliminate waste, mucus and toxemias, and this system assists Nature in the most perfect and natural way Not the disease but the body is to be healed; it must be cleansed, freed from waste and foreign matter, from mucus and toxemias accumulated since childhood.  You cannot buy health in a bottle, you cannot heal your body, that is, cleanse your system in a few days, you must make “compensation” for the wrong you have done your body all during your life.  My system is not a cure or a remedy; it is a regeneration, a thorough house-cleaning, the acquisition of such clean and perfect health as you never knew before.  Remember: Your constitutional encumbrances throughout the entire system are the source of every disease; the greatest and most harmful source of lowered vitality, imperfect health, lack of strength and endurance and any and all imperfect conditions.  All have their source in the colon, never perfectly emptied since your birth."
