    "fullText": "Lahmann said: “Every disease is caused by carbonic acid and gas”. — Naturopathic Concepts Naturopathy is an advance over medicine in teaching that all disease is constitutional.  Naturopathy does not explain sufficiently the source, nature and composition of “foreign matters” as the fundamental one-ness of all disease.  Dr.  Lahmann said: “Every disease is caused by carbonic acid and gas”.  But he did not learn its source in decayed, uneliminated food substances-the mucus in a state of continuous fermentation.  Dr.  Jaeger said: “Disease is a stench”.  Nature gives a diagnosis thru bad odor, which indicates how far the inside decomposition has progressed.  Dr.  Haigh of England, the founder of the “Anti-uric acid diet”, bases his conception of general diagnose on the assumption that the majority of diseases are caused thru uric acid, certainly an important part of diseased matter besides mucus.  Naturopathy lays considerable stress and importance on symptomatical diagnosis in spite of the acknowledgment that there is only one disease."
