    "fullText": "“science”. — Second—The presence of sugar-stuff in the blood.  That great expert of physiological chemistry and mineral salt theory founder, Hensel, says in his book “Life”: “Iron is chemically veiled in our blood. ” Doctors could not find it through their lack of knowledge in chemistry.  On page 36 of the same book he says: “In our blood albumen is a combination of sugar-stuff and iron oxide, but not to be found or recognized (discovered) in such a way that neither the sugar nor the iron can be found by ordinary chemical tests.  The blood albumen must be burned first to make the test perfect. ” I presume that the truth and importance is this: The red color of blood is the most characteristic quality of this “quite special sap” and is due to iron-oxide, rust!  Therefore, it is self-evident how important iron is in the blood."
