    "fullText": "Confusion in Dietetics L ESSON XI. — This is tremendously manifested by Nature thru the simple fact that every animal refuses food when sick.  The animal instinct of responding to every disease or even accident by fasting is Nature's demonstration that health and disease depend mainly and entirely from eating or not eating, as well as the kind of foods.  That the average man, and even the reformed doctors, blame everything on earth, excepting food, as the cause of their disease is due to the tragical fact that disease is as yet a mystery in their minds.  They don't know (and speaking for the doctors, they don't want to learn), how terribly unclean the inside of the body is, caused thru the life-long habit of over-eating ten times as much as required—in many cases harmful foods mostly, or even exclusively."
