    "fullText": "Confusion in Dietetics L ESSON XI. — H OW THE C OMBINATION OF D IFFERENT F OODS HAS TO BE A RRANGED .  3.  H OW L ONG AND HOW O FTEN F ASTING M UST BE I NTRODUCED AND C OMBINED D URING THE H EALING D IET IF F OUND N ECESSARY .  This is and represents the “SYSTEM” of the Mucusless Diet and Fasting as well as what the Practitioner has to study and must learn , and what the layman does not know and consequently why he must inevitably fail when trying to cure himself with “good foods”.  After the foregoing explanation you will at once see in the following critique of the best known dietetics, why they are imperfect, and why the confusion is so great.  In later lessons you will also learn of every kind of food, why it is good, and why bad.  In case you are still unaware of the foods which are mucusless, and which mucus-forming, they are as follows: All fruits, raw or cooked; also nuts and green-leaf vegetables are mucus-free."
