    "fullText": "D RINK THE J UICE O NLY . — The bananas would be for a less “mucused” or less acid stomach.  Menus for the Second Two Weeks L UNCH : First a baked apple, apple sauce or other stewed dried fruit.  After ten or fifteen minutes a combination salad as suggested in first menu, and bran or whole wheat bread toasted if still hungry.  Cow butter should be gradually avoided and replaced by a vegetable or nut butter during the transition.  By allowing the cooked vegetables to soak on the salad for 10 to 15 minutes it serves the purpose of a dressing.  S UPPER : A baked or stewed vegetable as suggested in the first menu, followed with a vegetable salad made of lettuce and cucumber or raw celery or a little coleslaw.  Menus for the Third Two Weeks L UNCH : During the summer this should be an exclusive fruit meal-one kind only."
