    "excerpt": "For a bad, acid or “mucused stomach” use menus consisting of more vegetables and very little fruits.  For a stomach in better condition, or the average stomach, use more fruits and less vegetables.  The following is an example: 1.  F OR A B AD S TOMACH : Take as stock grated or shredded raw carrots, or grated celery or...",
    "fullText": "Transition Diet (Continued) L ESSON XVI. — For a bad, acid or “mucused stomach” use menus consisting of more vegetables and very little fruits.  For a stomach in better condition, or the average stomach, use more fruits and less vegetables.  The following is an example: 1.  F OR A B AD S TOMACH : Take as stock grated or shredded raw carrots, or grated celery or grated beets may be used, altho carrots are best.  Add of finely sliced very ripe bananas and a few raisins or sliced dried figs.  No nuts or cereals.  N EVER M IX N UTS WITH W ET F RUIT .  2.  F OR A B ETTER S TOMACH : Take as stock sliced or grated apples, shredded carrots (or celery or beets).  To increase the efficiency of this combination in its aggressive, dissolving functions as a mucus and poison eliminator add more raisins, sliced dried figs, honey or a fruit jelly.  Fruit acid dissolves waste and forms gases; fruit sugar ferments in the waste and stirs up, also forming gases."
