    "fullText": "It is yet in the shade of a mystery. — Procreation is the most holy and divine act and charged with the highest responsibility, especially on the part of the father.  A germ with the slightest defect is a generation not forward but downward.  In very old and in classic civilization “Sex” was a cult, a religion, and in every mystology, poetry of all civilized people, love is the great, main and general subject with the conscious or unconscious goal to reproduce his kind.  The fact is proven by statistics that every family of the city's population dies out, disappears with the third or fourth generation.  In other words, the “sins” of the fathers and of the mothers produce diseased children and children's children degenerating into death with the third generation.  What are these “sins”?  You shall “love thy neighbor”, and you do, perhaps, but you kill your own child, partly at least before it is born.  Latent disease is general and universal."
