    "fullText": "“Peace on Earth” happiness and righteousness as yet remain a foolish dream. — “Peace on Earth” happiness and righteousness as yet remain a foolish dream.  During thousands of years, God, Paradise, Heaven—Sin, Devil, Hell—seldom found an interpretation that a clear, reasoning mind would willingly accept.  The average unfortunate fellowman thinks of God as a good and forgiving Father who will allow him to enter Paradise in another world—unpunished for any violations of His laws in Nature.  I have proven for the first time in history that the diet of Paradise is not only possible —good enough for a degenerate mankind, such as we now are—but that it is the Unconditional Necessity and the first step to real salvation and redemption from the misery of life.  That it is a needed key to the lost Paradise where disease, worry and sorrow—hate, fighting and murder were unknown, and where there was no death, from unnatural causes at least.  “Man is what he eats” is a philosopher's greatest and truest statement."
