    "fullText": "6. Ajos Sacha ( Pseudocalymma alliaceum ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : ajos sacha, sacha ajos, ajo sacha, aboeja-mibia, ah-kah-pota, ajo machoajosacha, ajos del monte, Amazonian garlic bush, ayotete, be'o-ho, be'o-ja pusanga, bejuco de ajo, boens, cipo-alho, cipo-d’alho, false garlic, garlic rope, garlic vine, gonofroe-tite, ilay kamwi, ka ale, knof-looklian, knoflook liaan, koenofrokoetite, kwi-po-kan, liane-ail, nia boens, nishi boains, posatalu, sacha ajo, sucho ajo, shansque boains, tingi-tite, vova, wild garlic, woe-ipole - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Immunité & Anti-infectieux (Immunomodulateur & Antiviral) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Ajos Sacha Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/mansoa.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - Ajos sacha is rich in polyphenols (flavonoids  - anthocyanins  - phenolic acids  - and tannins)  - ketones  - triterpenes  - as well as other bioactive compounds  - Ajos sacha - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - the leaves  - vine bark  - and root  - The leaves  - tied in bunches  - Oftentimes - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : The sulfur compounds (the predominate ones being alliin and various allyl sulfides) in both garlic and ajos sacha have been studied by many and reported over the years to be able to lower cholesterol. When laboratory rats were fed dried ajos sacha flowers (2% of their dietary intake), scientists reported that cholesterol levels were lowered, and much like garlic, the absorption of cholesterol in t... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Ajos sacha is well used and respected by most of the indigenous Indian tribes of the Amazon and almost all parts of the plant are used; the leaves, vine bark, and root. Most consider the plant to be “magical” or “spiritual” and capable of driving away evil spirits or used for good luck. The leaves, tied in bunches, can often be found in local huts ... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : relieves pain kills bacteria Leaf or Bark reduces inflammation kills fungi Decoction: 1 cup 2-3 times daily fights free radicals kills head lice Tincture: 3-4 ml twice daily relieves oxidative stress kills parasites Capsules: 1-2 g twice daily reduces fever protects heart eases colds & flu prevents atherosclerosis kills viruses reduces spasms lowers blood pressure protects cells & organs  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - None reported. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
