    "fullText": "9. Amor seco ( Desmodium adscendens ) — - Famille Botanique : Plante Amazonienne - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Amor seco - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Amor seco Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/amorseco.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - Amor seco is known to be rich in flavonoids  - alkaloids  - glycosides and chemicals known as soyasaponins  - A novel soyasaponin in amor seco is dehydrosoyasaponin 1  - It is considered a highly active chemical with therapeutic actions for asthma  - Amor seco also contains a chemical called astragalin  - Amor seco’s traditional uses for infections  - venereal diseases - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - Today  - A tea of the plant is given for nervousness  - and it is used in baths to treat vaginal infections  - Some tribes believe the plant has magic powers  - and it is taken by lovers to rekindle a waning romance  - an application of pounded leaves and lime juice for wounds - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Herbalists in Ghana have long used amor seco leaves to treat bronchial asthma. The treatment was so successful that it attracted attention from the scientific community. In 1977, a clinical observational study on humans showed that 1 to 2 teaspoons of dried amor seco leaf powder daily (in three dosages) produced improvement and remission in most asthma patients treated. In an effort to understand ... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Today, tribes in the Amazon rainforest use amor seco medicinally much as they have for centuries. A tea of the plant is given for nervousness, and it is used in baths to treat vaginal infections. Some tribes believe the plant has magic powers, and it is taken by lovers to rekindle a waning romance. Rio Pastaza natives in the Amazon brew a leaf tea ... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : relieves pain cleanses blood Leaves, Whole herb blocks allergies detoxifies Infusion: 1-3 cups daily relieves asthma increases urination Tincture: 4-5 ml daily reduces convulsions mildly laxative capsules: 3-4 g daily blocks histamine heals wounds reduces inflammation calms stress reduces spasms stops bleeding dilates bronchials relaxes muscles protects cells scavenges free radicals  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Do not take in high dosages. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
