    "fullText": "15. Bellaco-Caspi ( Plumeria sucuuba, floribunda ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Bellaco-Caspi - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Immunité & Anti-infectieux (Immunomodulateur & Antiviral) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Bellaco-Caspi Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/himatanthus.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - In addition  - These two chemicals have been reported with cytotoxic  - anti-cancerous  - anti-fungal and anti-bacterial actions in laboratory research  - magnesium  - arabinose  - xylose  - rhamnose and galactose - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - pain and/or inflammation  - as well as put the latex directly onto abscesses  - sores  - and skin ulcers  - It is considered a pain-reliever  - blood cleanser - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Many of bellaco caspi's traditional uses are being verified in preliminary studies and laboratory research. Thus far, research has confirmed that bellaco caspi has antibacterial, anti-fungal, anthelmintic, anti-leishmanial, anti-inflammatory, analgesic, anti-depressant, immunoregulatory, cytotoxic, and genotoxic actions. In 2005, Brazilian researchers verified bellaco caspi's traditional use for s... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : The bark and the latex of bellaco caspi have a long history of use among the Indians in the Amazon. The Karijonas powder the tree bark and sprinkle it directly onto stubborn wounds and sores. The Shipibo-Conibo Indians in Peru prepare a decoction of the bark and take it internally for rheumatism and body aches and pain. They also put the latex in w... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : relieves pain reduces fever Bark reduces inflammation calms coughs Decoction: 1 cup twice daily kills bacteria & viruses cleanses blood Capsules: 1 g 2 - 3 kills fungi/candida expels worms times daily flushes lymph glands detoxifies Tincture: 2-4 ml twice daily heals wounds kills cancer cells prevents/heals ulcers aids menstruation fights free radicals protects organs  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Consulter un professionnel de santé en cas de grossesse, allaitement ou traitement médical lourd. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
