    "fullText": "24. Calumba ( Jateorhiza palmata ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Calumba, calumba root, columba, colombo, kalumba, kalumb, jateorhiza, guvercin koku otu - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Foie & Digestion (Hépato-Biliaire & Détox) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Calumba Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/calumba.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - Calumba root contains 2-3% total alkaloids  - chiefly protoberberines (palmatine  - jatrorrhizine  - columbamine)  - Several of these alkaloids have a narcotic effect similar to morphine  - Other chemical include: alkaloids  - bisjatrorrhizine  - chasmanthin - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - with pain or without pain  - immediately upon eating  - low stomach acid  - diarrhea  - and loss of appetite - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Researchers in Japan conducted a study in 2002 with rats. They extracted a chemical from calumba root called columbin and fed it to rats in very low dosages. They reported that this compound was able to prevent colon cancer stating: \"These results indicate chemopreventive ability of dietary columbin against chemically induced colon tumorigenesis when fed during the initiation phase, providing a sc... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : The root of this tropical plant is used in traditional medicine systems world wide. It was first recorded in herbal medicine in 1671 when Portuguese traders took the plant from Africa back to Europe. Calumba root has long held a place in herbal medicine as a gentle but very effective digestive bitter. Bitters work on the principal that a bitter tas... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : aids digestion increases bile Root expels gas dries secretions Infusion: 1 cup 3 times daily reduces nausea kills germs Tincture: 1-2 ml twice daily relieves diarrhea  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Consulter un professionnel de santé en cas de grossesse, allaitement ou traitement médical lourd. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
