    "fullText": "38. Chuchuhuasi ( Maytenus krukovii ) — - Famille Botanique : Plante Amazonienne - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Chuchuhuasi - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Foie & Digestion (Hépato-Biliaire & Détox) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Chuchuhuasi Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/chuchuhuasi.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - Chuchuhuasi is a powerhouse of plant chemicals-mostly triterpenes  - polyphenol flavonols  - and sesquiterpene alkaloids  - While these chemicals are found in chuchuhuasi  - Another rainforest Maytenus plant  - espinheira santa (also featured in this book)  - is a much better source of these anticancerous chemicals  - which are some of the tree bark’s active constituents - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - Its Peruvian name  - chuchuhuasi  - means \"trembling back  - \" which refers to its long-standing use for arthritis  - rheumatism  - and back pain - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Chuchuhuasi's long history of use has fueled much clinical interest in the research community. In the 1960s, an American pharmaceutical company discovered potent immune-stimulating properties of a leaf extract and a bark extract, documenting that it increased phagocytosis (the ability of immune cells to attack bacteria and foreign cells) in mice. Researchers in 1977 reported that alcohol extracts ... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Indigenous people of the Amazon rainforest have been using the bark of chuchuhuasi medicinally for centuries. Its Peruvian name, chuchuhuasi, means \"trembling back,\" which refers to its long-standing use for arthritis, rheumatism, and back pain. One local Indian remedy for arthritis and rheumatism calls for one cup of a bark decoction taken three t... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : reduces inflammation kills cancer cells Bark relieves pain prevents tumors Decoction: 1 cup 2-3 times daily relaxes muscles stimulates digestion Tincture: 3-5 ml 2-3 times daily enhances immune function balances hormones increases libido reduces depression supports adrenals calms anxiety fights free radicals kills bacteria & viruses relieves oxidative stress protects organs  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - None reported. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
