    "fullText": "52. Damiana ( Turnera aphrodisiaca ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Damiana - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Damiana Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/damiana.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - 8-cineole  - p-cymene  - alpha- and beta-pinene  - thymol  - alpha-copaene  - and calamene)  - Damiana leaves also contain tannins  - flavonoids - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - as well as for \"giddiness and loss of balance  - added sugar  - and drank it for its purported power to enhance lovemaking  - It is thought to act as an aphrodisiac  - antidepressant  - tonic - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Damiana has demonstrated mild hypoglycemic effects in animals. Persons with diabetes and hypoglycemia should use this plant with caution, as blood sugar levels should be monitored accordingly for this possible effect. Damiana has a traditional use as an abortive and is contraindicated during pregnancy. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Only one clinical study has been conducted to validate the traditional use of the plant for sexual dysfunction and impotence. In 1999, a group of researchers in Italy administered damiana to both sexually potent and sexually sluggish (or impotent) rats. The extract had no effect on sexually potent rats but, in the others, it increased the percentage of rats achieving ejaculation and made them more... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Damiana was recorded to be used as an aphrodisiac in the ancient Mayan civilization, as well as for \"giddiness and loss of balance.\" A Spanish missionary first reported that the Mexican Indians made a drink from the damiana leaves, added sugar, and drank it for its purported power to enhance lovemaking. Damiana has a long history of use in traditio... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : increases libido reduces spasms Leaves relieves depression dries secretions Infusion: 1 cup 2-3 times daily reduces blood sugar stimulates digestion Fluid Extract: 2-4 ml twice daily calms nerves increases urination Capsules: 3-4 g twice daily mildly laxative  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Damiana has demonstrated mild hypoglycemic effects in animals. Persons with diabetes and hypoglycemia should use this plant with caution, as blood sugar levels should be monitored accordingly for this possible effect. Damiana has a traditional use as an abortive and is contraindicated during pregnancy. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
