    "fullText": "67. Guayusa ( Ilex guayusa ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Guayusa - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Guayusa Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/guayusa.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - Guayusa has a similar chemical makeup of its closely related “cousin  - ” yerba mate  - Both are significant sources of caffeine  - with guayusa providing a bit more  - Guayusa leaves contain 1  - 73–3  - 48% caffeine (compared to 0  - 7–2% in yerba mate and 1–2 - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - ulcers  - heart diseases  - and other diseases  - Guayusa might lower blood sugar levels  - anxiety  - fast heart rate  - and more - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Guayusa contains caffeine and should not be used by those who are sensitive or allergic to caffeine. Excessive consumption of caffeine is contraindicated for persons with high blood pressure, ulcers, heart diseases, and other diseases. Guayusa might lower blood sugar levels. Diabetics need to monitor their glucose levels to determine if their medications need adjusting or seek the guidance of their health care provider. Guayusa tea should be consumed in moderation to avoid caffeine’s side effects such as insomnia, anxiety, fast heart rate, and more. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Guayusa has evidenced anti-diabetic and hypoglycemic actions in test tube and animal studies. Its main mechanism of action to lower blood sugar levels is to interfere with two digestive enzymes that break down sugar so it can be absorbed (alpha- and beta-glucosidases) during the digestive process. If it is not broken down, then it (and its calories) is simply eliminated and not absorbed. This mech... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Indigenous tribes and local people in the Amazon cultivate guayusa in their villages or along the edges of their garden areas. One of four known caffeinated holly trees, the leaves of the guayusa tree are harvested fresh and brewed like a tea for their stimulative effects. It is a close relative to another stimulant holly tree, yerba mate . It is k... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : increase energy reduces pain Leaves promotes weight loss increases urination Tincture: 2 ml three times daily suppresses appetite reduces blood pressure Decoction: 1 cup 3 times daily burns fat protects brain Capsules: 1 g 3 times daily reduces inflammation relieves depression &nbsp modulates immune system reduces blood sugar prevents chronic diseases increases fertility protects organs fights free radicals avoids diabetic complications relieves oxidative stress  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Consulter un professionnel de santé en cas de grossesse, allaitement ou traitement médical lourd. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
