    "fullText": "72. Iporuru ( Alchornea castaneifolia ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Iporuru, iporoni, iporuro, ipururo, ipurosa, macochihua, niando, pajaro - Parties Utilisées : Leaves, bark, roots - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Immunité & Anti-infectieux (Immunomodulateur & Antiviral) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Iporuru Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/iporuru.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - Initial screening has revealed it to contain steroids  - saponins  - phenols  - flavonols  - flavones  - tannins  - xanthones  - and alkaloids - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - sometimes  - is an ingredient in ayahuasca (a hallucinogenic  - multi-herb decoction used by South American shamans)  - called aguardiente ) as a local remedy for rheumatism  - arthritis  - colds - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Likewise, there has been little clinical research on iporuru - despite its long history of use in South American herbal medicine. That which has been done, however, does help explain some of its traditional uses. Pharmacognosy students in Sweden documented that an ethanol extract of the stembark was capable of reducing lab-induced swelling and inflammation in rats when applied topically. These res... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : For centuries the indigenous peoples of the Amazon have used the bark and leaves of iporuru for many different purposes and prepared it in many different ways. The plant commonly is used with other plants during shamanistic training and, sometimes, is an ingredient in ayahuasca (a hallucinogenic, multi-herb decoction used by South American shamans)... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : relieves pain kills fungi Leaves reduces inflammation kills viruses Infusion: 1 cup 2-3 kills cancer cells kills viruses times daily increases libido prevents tumors Maceration: 1/2 cup 2-3 times daily  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - None known. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
