    "fullText": "78. Jergon Sacha ( Dracontium loretense ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Jerg&oacute, n sacha, fer-de-lance, sacha jergon, hierba del jergon, erva-jararaca, jararaca, jararaca-taia, milho-de-cobra, taja-de-cobra - Parties Utilisées : Tuber/rhizome - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Jergon Sacha Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/jergon.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - Initial phytochemical screening indicates that the rhizome contains alkaloids  - flavonoids  - phenols  - saponins  - sterols  - triterpenes  - and starch  - none of these have been quantified or identified - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - Ethnobotanically  - In this particular case  - In Peru and Ecuador  - In Brazil the snake is named jararaca  - the plant  - erva-jararaca (jararaca herb) - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Despite the large and growing market for jergón sacha, not a single clinical study has been published on its actions. If jergón sacha's longstanding use as an effective snakebite remedy was clinically validated, it may explain its more recent use as an antiviral for HIV as well. The most recent class of drugs developed for HIV are called protease inhibitors . Protease inhibitors work by blocking a... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Ethnobotanically, jergón sacha is considered a \"signature plant\": the plant's indigenous uses are directly related to its appearance. In this particular case, the trunk-like stem and its mottled coloring closely resembles a poisonous snake indigenous to the areas in which it grows. In Peru and Ecuador, the name of both snake and plant is jergón sac... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : kills viruses calms coughs Rhizome neutralizes venom expels worms Capsules: 2-3 g 2-3 times daily reduces inflammation Tincture: 3-5 ml twice daily  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Consulter un professionnel de santé en cas de grossesse, allaitement ou traitement médical lourd. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
