    "fullText": "79. Juazeiro ( Zizyphus joazeiro ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Juazeiro - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Juazeiro Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/juazeiro.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - Juazeiro contains many active plant chemicals  - including phlobaphenic tannins  - flavonoids  - leucoanthocyanidins  - flavanones  - catechins  - alkaloids  - steroids - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - the fruit is edible and sometimes turned into wine  - the bark and leaves are used medicinally  - and the wood is very durable and used for making furniture  - farm implements  - artistic wood carvings  - and charcoal - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Although its mechanism is still unknown, scientists have verified juazeiro's main traditional use for fevers. In a study with rabbits, the oral administration of a bark infusion reduced fevers that had been induced by bacterial toxins. In Brazilian research, scientists have validated its use for dental cavities; a bark decoction demonstrated strong activity against the common bacteria that forms d... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Juazeiro is one of the most respected trees in Brazil due to its numerous uses. The leaves and young branches are used as a high protein animal fodder (especially during severe droughts when not much else is available); the fruit is edible and sometimes turned into wine, the bark and leaves are used medicinally; and the wood is very durable and use... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : reduces fever heals wounds Bark kills bacteria increases urination Decoction: 1/2 cup 2-3 prevents cavities supports heart times daily reduces plaque protects gastric tract Tincture: Applied topically suppresses coughs kills viruses fights free radicals kills parasites relieves oxidative stress kills fungi  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - None known. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
