    "fullText": "83. Maidenhair Fern ( Adiantum capillus-veneris ) — - Famille Botanique : Pteridaceae - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Maidenhair Fern - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Maidenhair Fern Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/avenca.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - triterpenoids  - flavonoids  - phenyl propanoids  - coumarins  - phytosterols  - fatty acids and others  - diabetes  - liver disorders - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - In European herbal medicine  - Dioscorides  - a famous Greek physician  - wrote De Materia Medica  - a five-part treatise on more than 600 medicinal plants  - including avenca - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Avenca’s antibacterial and antifungal actions have been well studied in over 20 different in vitro studies and in one animal study published between 1980 and 2019. Interestingly, the strongest antibacterial and antifungal actions come from just a simple water extract of avenca’s fronds. When researchers tried other extraction methods using ethanol, methanol and hexane, the antibacterial action was... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Avenca has held a place in herbal medicine systems for almost 2,000 years in the many countries around the world where it grows. In European herbal medicine, its documented use predates the era of Dioscorides and Pliny (23 to 79 A.D.). Dioscorides, a famous Greek physician, wrote De Materia Medica, a five-part treatise on more than 600 medicinal pl... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : suppresses coughs eliminates stones Leaves or rhizome reduces phlegm protects liver Infusion: 1/2 cup twice daily kills viruses reduces cholesterol Tincture: 1-3 ml twice daily kills bacteria reduces blood pressure Capsules: 2 g twice daily kills fungi and yeast stimulates fights free radicals supports gallbladder promotes weight loss heals wounds detoxifies dries secretions increases urination stimulates menstruation lowers blood sugar inhibits cancer reduces inflammation reduces pain relieves oxidative stress  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Consulter un professionnel de santé en cas de grossesse, allaitement ou traitement médical lourd. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
