    "fullText": "91. Murure ( Brosimum acutifolium ) — - Famille Botanique :  - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Murure - Parties Utilisées : Feuilles, écorce, racines ou plante entière - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Immunité & Anti-infectieux (Immunomodulateur & Antiviral) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Murure Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/tamamuri.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - Tamamuri bark contains polyphenols (flavans  - flavanoids  - chalcones  - and lignans)  - phenylpropanoids  - benezoids  - and steroids  - Many of these chemicals are novel ones never before seen by scientists - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - to purify the blood and to regulate the nervous system  - It is also a very common remedy for syphilis  - which is how it earned one of its common names  - \"vegetable mercury  - tamamuri is considered a pain-reliever  - anti-inflammatory - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Tamamuri's long-standing use for arthritis and rheumatism has been the subject of research by Western scientists. In 2003, Brazilian researchers reported that crude extracts of tamamuri bark reduced inflammation induced by various means in laboratory rats. Other researchers have reported that two chemicals in tamamuri ( mururin A and B) have the ability to inhibit protein kinase C (PKC) and protei... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : Shipibo-Conibo Indians on the Ucayali River in the Peruvian Amazon have a legend about tamamuri. They believe that when a man ingests the white latex of the tamamuri tree that he will father light-skinned male children. They also use the bark medicinally (in decoctions) for gastro-intestinal disorders, to purify the blood and to regulate the nervou... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : eases arthritis increases libido Bark reduces inflammation expels worms Tincture: 2 ml three times daily relieves pain kills cancer cells Decoction: 1 cup 3 times daily kills fungi/yeast kills leukemia cells Capsules: 1 g 3 times daily kills bacteria cleanses blood fights free radicals overall tonic relieves oxidative stress prevents ulcers  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - Tamamuri contains two plant chemicals with documented estrogenic actions in animal studies. Women with estrogen-positive cancers should avoid the use of tamamuri until further research confirms tamamuri's effect on estrogen. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
