    "fullText": "111. Scarlet Bush ( Hamelia patens ) — - Famille Botanique : Rubiaceae - Noms Usuels / Synonymes : Scarlet bush, fire bush, Texas firecracker, corail - Parties Utilisées : Leaves - Catégorie Thérapeutique & Tropisme : Reins & Émonctoires (Drainage Rénal & Lithiases) - Source Primaire Rain-Tree : [Scarlet Bush Monograph on Rain-Tree.com](https://www.rain-tree.com/scarletbush.htm) - Principes Phytochimiques Actifs :  - both have been highly studied and even patented as effective immune stimulants  - anxiety  - eating disorders  - chronic pain conditions and obesity  - they've been named Hamelia patens alkaloid A  - B and C  - In addition  - the aerial parts of the plant have been found to contain rosmarinic acid - Indications & Cibles Thérapeutiques :  - It's Mayan name  - Ix-canan  - means \"guardian of the forest  - sores  - rashes  - wounds - Mécanismes & Pharmacodynamie (Leslie Taylor) : 1. Actions Principales (Rain-Tree) : Documenté par Leslie Taylor pour ses principes phytochimiques actifs. 2. Recherche Clinique & Activité Biologique : Much of the clinical research on scarlet bush has validated the traditional uses of the plant. In animal studies (with rats) scarlet bush leaf extracts demonstrated analgesic, diuretic, and hypothermic actions. External use of the leaf in mice showed significant anti-inflammatory activity comparable to that of a prescription anti-inflammatory drug used as a control. Scientists in two different cou... 3. Usage Ethnobotanique Traditionnel : It's Mayan name, Ix-canan , means \"guardian of the forest.\" Indigenous people in Belize use the plant to prepare a natural remedy to treat all types of skin problems including, sores, rashes, wounds, burns, itching, cuts, skin fungus, and insect stings and bites. The remedy is prepared by boiling a double handful of leaves, stems and flowers in 2 g... - Posologie & Modes d'Administration :  - Dosage Standard : relieves pain reduces spasms Leaves reduces inflammation kills parasites Infusion: 1 cup 2-3 heals wounds enhances immunity times daily kills bacteria increases urination Tincture: 1-2 ml twice daily reduces fever increases urination kills fungi lowers body temperature  - Infusion / Décoction : 1 cuillère à café à soupe de plante séchée par tasse d'eau chaude, infuser 10-15 min.  - Teinture : 2 à 4 ml (environ 30 à 60 gouttes) 2 fois par jour. - Contre-indications & Précautions :  - None known. - Note Vitaliste : Fiche botanique officielle Rain-Tree issue des recherches du Dr. Leslie Taylor sur la pharmacopée amazonienne.  ---"
